 The manual `Export RCC Preparation Review Evidence` workflow is a read-only access path for the larger canonical preparation artifact. It accepts an existing preparation run ID, source SHA, version, and manifest SHA; verifies that the selected source is in the current main history; uses only `actions: read` and `contents: read`; rechecks the exact successful preparation run, all required job results, GitHub's ZIP digest, the prepared bundle, and actual Go 1.26.9 binary metadata; then uploads a source-bound evidence-only sidecar capped at 24 MiB raw. The sidecar includes the original full ZIP digest, asset manifest/checksums/provenance, numeric full11 exit and task receipt, self-host and N-1 receipts, four native runtime receipts and Robot XML, and Linux JAT receipt. It excludes distribution binaries, the N-1 archive, and private home materializations. It does not create a release, tag, or Homebrew dispatch and cannot replace or alter the canonical preparation artifact consumed by the publisher.
 
-Publication requires the `rcc-production` environment to exist and have exactly one required-reviewers rule, at least one reviewer, self-review prevention, and admin bypass disabled. The publisher queries that policy and fails closed if it cannot read it. Configure `RCC_RELEASE_POLICY_AUDIT_TOKEN` as a repository secret containing a fine-grained token or GitHub App token with repository **Administration: read** permission so the environment API can be inspected. The workflow job itself must remain attached to the protected environment; the API check does not replace GitHub's approval gate. The person dispatching publication cannot approve their own run, so a different authorized reviewer must review and approve the pending job. A missing token, insufficient permission, absent environment, or unreadable protection configuration blocks publication.
+Publication requires the `rcc-production` environment to exist and have exactly one required-reviewers rule, at least one reviewer, and admin bypass disabled. Self-review prevention remains the default. The approved sole-maintainer exception applies only to `joshyorko/rcc`, environment `rcc-production`, and exactly one User reviewer `joshyorko` (GitHub user ID54248591), with prevent_self_review=false. Josh may dispatch and manually approve that release; this retains approval but removes a second-person check. The publisher queries that policy and fails closed if it cannot read it. Configure `RCC_RELEASE_POLICY_AUDIT_TOKEN` as a repository secret containing a fine-grained token or GitHub App token with repository **Administration: read** permission so the environment API can be inspected. The workflow job must remain attached to the protected environment; the API check does not replace its manual approval gate. A missing token, insufficient permission, absent environment, unreadable protection, admin bypass or mismatched sole-maintainer identity blocks publication.
 
 The publisher also requires a separate `HOMEBREW_TOOLS_PAT` secret that can dispatch `tap-auto-update.yml` in `homebrew-tools`. Its current preflight proves only that the downstream workflow is readable and active; it does not prove the token has dispatch permission. Confirm that access separately before any publication. The repository's configured `GITHUB_TOKEN` must also be allowed to create a new tag and release. The publisher never deletes or replaces a tag or release and does not edit an existing release.
 
